---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About Drew Reitzel" description="Drew Reitzel is a prophetic writer and speaker calling the Church back to biblical fidelity. Author of You Can't Serve Two Masters.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Drew Reitzel",
    "url": "https://www.undividedallegiance.com/about/",
    "jobTitle": "Author, Writer, Speaker",
    "description": "Prophetic writer and speaker calling the Church back to biblical fidelity. Author of You Can't Serve Two Masters.",
    "knowsAbout": ["biblical theology", "cultural Christianity", "church integrity", "faith and culture"],
    "sameAs": [
      "https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61579550235172",
      "https://instagram.com/undividedallegiance",
      "https://www.tiktok.com/@undividedallegiance",
      "https://x.com/UndivAllegiance",
      "https://www.linkedin.com/company/undivided-allegiance",
      "https://youtube.com/@UndividedAllegiance"
    ],
    "author": {
      "@type": "Book",
      "name": "You Can't Serve Two Masters",
      "url": "https://www.undividedallegiance.com/book/"
    }
  })} />
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-black">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <span class="text-red text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] block mb-6">About</span>
        <h1 class="mb-6">The Voice Behind the Message</h1>
        <div class="divider mb-6"></div>
        <p class="text-muted-light text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          A prophetic writer and speaker calling the Church back to biblical fidelity — not from a place of arrival, but from a place of conviction.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bio -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2 class="text-3xl mb-8">Drew Reitzel</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-muted-light text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Drew Reitzel is a prophetic writer and speaker whose work sits at the intersection
            of faith, culture, and biblical truth. His writing does not seek to be popular.
            It seeks to be faithful.
          </p>
          <p>
            He holds a degree in theology and spent several years in pastoral ministry before
            entering the marketplace, where he spent more than two decades building businesses
            and learning what it costs to carry conviction in a world that rewards compromise.
            That tension, between what Scripture demands and what culture rewards, is where his
            writing was forged.
          </p>
          <p>
            In a time when the Church has learned to speak in softer tones to avoid offending
            the world, Drew writes with the conviction that truth spoken in love is never cruel.
            But silence in the face of compromise always is.
          </p>
          <p>
            He is not writing from a place of having arrived. He is writing from a place of
            conviction, shaped by his own failures, his own seasons of wandering, and his own
            experience of what it means to be pulled in two directions at once. That is what
            makes this message personal. And what makes it urgent.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Book -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-black">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <span class="text-red text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] block mb-4">The Book</span>
        <h2 class="mb-8">You Can't Serve Two Masters</h2>
        <div class="divider mb-8"></div>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-muted-light text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            After a year of writing, Drew released his debut book in April 2026. It is a
            theological examination of the allegiance crisis that has quietly gutted the
            American Church, and an invitation to come home whole.
          </p>
          <p>
            The book confronts the silencing of the pulpit, the redefinition of biblical truth
            to match cultural comfort, and the slow trade the Church has made: the authority of
            Scripture for the approval of the world. It names what most people in the pews
            already sense but cannot articulate. And it points toward the only way forward.
          </p>
          <p>
            Repentance is not shame. It is the door back to where God always intended His Church
            to stand. That is the message of this book. That is the message Drew has given his
            voice to.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8">
            <a href="/book/" class="btn-primary inline-flex">
              Read About the Book
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <path d="M7 17L17 7M17 7H7M17 7v10"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Mission -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-black">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <span class="text-red text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] block mb-4">The Mission</span>
        <h2 class="mb-8">Why Undivided Allegiance Exists</h2>
        <div class="divider mb-8"></div>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-muted-light text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            Undivided Allegiance exists for the remnant — the believers who sense that something
            has gone deeply wrong in the modern Church but struggle to find voices willing to
            name it clearly.
          </p>
          <p>
            This is not about being right. It is about being faithful. The darkness of the hour
            is real — but so is the light that refuses to go out.
          </p>
          <p>
            Every essay, every episode, every word published here serves one purpose: to call
            the Church back to the standard it was given and the God it was made for.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Values -->
  <section class="section-padding bg-charcoal">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="fade-in">
        <h2 class="mb-12 text-center">What We Stand On</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
          {[
            { title: 'Biblical Authority', text: 'Scripture is not a suggestion. It is the immovable foundation on which everything else must be tested.' },
            { title: 'Prophetic Honesty', text: 'We speak what is true, not what is comfortable. Love without truth is sentimentality. Truth without love is cruelty.' },
            { title: 'Cultural Clarity', text: 'We name what the culture celebrates and what Scripture confronts — without apology and without malice.' },
            { title: 'Remnant Identity', text: 'This is for those who have counted the cost. The narrow road is narrow for a reason.' },
          ].map((value) => (
            <div class="p-8 border border-cream/5">
              <h3 class="text-xl mb-4 text-cream">{value.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">{value.text}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
